  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How much does radiator installation cost in Liverpool?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A standard double panel rad, supplied and fitted, costs from £200. This covers the rad, the TRV and a system balance on the day. Labour only for a like-for-like swap starts at £80. TRVs from £50 each. Relocation from £150. Column and designer rads are quoted on request. We give a written fixed-price quote first." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How long does radiator installation take in Liverpool?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A like-for-like single radiator swap takes 1 to 2 hours. A new radiator addition with pipework takes 2 to 4 hours. Multiple radiators can often be completed in a single day. A full house TRV upgrade typically takes half a day. We confirm the expected duration when we quote." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can you change a radiator to a bigger or smaller size?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. We can swap an undersized rad for a bigger one to warm a cold room. Or fit a smaller rad in a room that gets too hot. We work out the BTU output the room needs first. Then we pick a rad that hits that number. A right-sized rad is more energy efficient. You burn less gas for the same warm room." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can you add an additional radiator to my existing Liverpool heating system?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Adding a rad to your existing system takes 2 to 4 hours. We extend the circuit to the new spot and fit the rad with a TRV. We balance the system after. Most extension, loft conversion and conservatory jobs need at least one extra rad." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can you relocate a radiator in a Liverpool Victorian property?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. We drain down the circuit, reroute the pipework to the new position and rebalance the system. Relocation starts from £150 depending on distance and pipework. In Liverpool's older homes with solid walls, pipework is usually run under suspended timber floors or surface-mounted in neat boxing." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is a TRV and do I need one?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A thermostatic radiator valve controls the heat output of an individual radiator, allowing different temperatures in different rooms. Under Boiler Plus regulations, TRVs are required on all new radiator installations. They reduce heating bills by 10 to 15%. We fit TRVs from £50 per valve. One radiator in the house should be left without a TRV to act as a bypass." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need a power flush before fitting new radiators?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "If your existing radiators have cold spots at the bottom or the system water is brown or black when bled, a power flush is strongly recommended before fitting new radiators. A contaminated circuit will fill new radiators with sludge quickly. We assess the system condition at the quote visit and advise honestly on whether a flush is needed." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What radiator brands do you fit?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "We fit rads from Stelrad, Quinn, Myson, Reina, Hudson Reed, Bisque and Carron. Standard panel rads, designer rads and period-style rads all in the range. We can supply the rad or fit one you have bought. Tell us your budget and style and we will help you pick." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Are you Gas Safe registered?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is Gas Safe registered. All radiator work connecting to the heating circuit is done by our own directly employed Gas Safe heating engineers. Verify at gassaferegister.co.uk. We never use sub-contractors." } }
    ]
  }
  </script>

