  <!-- TYPES OF RADIATOR -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Types of Radiator We Supply and Fit in Liverpool</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We supply and fit every type of radiator found in Liverpool homes. Panel rads. Column rads. Designer rads. Towel rails. Low surface temp rads. All in one firm.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Standard panel radiators</strong><p>Single and double panel rads are the most common type across Liverpool. Double convector (type 22) rads give the most heat for their size. We fit these in most Liverpool rooms. They come in all standard lengths and heights.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Column radiators</strong><p>Column rads suit Liverpool's older homes well. They look right with the period style. We fit steel column rads in two, three and four-column versions. Heights run from 600mm to 1800mm. The right size matters. We work out the heat output the room needs before we suggest a model.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Designer and flat panel radiators</strong><p>Vertical designer rads are good for rooms where wall space is tight. We fit designer rads in all standard sizes. We advise on output before we order. Some designer rads with low surface area can under-perform in big Liverpool rooms if not sized right.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Bathroom and towel radiators</strong><p>Heated towel rails and bathroom rads come in chrome, white and anthracite. We can wire them to your central heating circuit. Or fit a dual-fuel version that works on its own. Handy for Liverpool homes where the bathroom is not always on with the rest.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Underfloor heating coexistence</strong><p>Got underfloor in some rooms and rads in others? We can run the rad circuit into rooms the underfloor system does not reach. Common in Liverpool extensions and new kitchens.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Low surface temperature radiators</strong><p>Low surface temp (LST) rads are a must in care homes. They are smart for rooms with young kids or older adults too. The rad surface stays below 43 degrees no matter the water temp. We fit LST rads in any Liverpool home where they are needed.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NEW: RADIATOR BRAND TIERS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">RADIATOR BRAND GUIDE</span>
      <h2>Radiator Brands We Fit. Standard, Designer and Period.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We fit rads from every major UK brand. Pick the right one for your budget and your style.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3 style="color:var(--navy);font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Standard Panel: Stelrad, Quinn and Myson</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.6;">Standard panel rads from Stelrad, Quinn and Myson. Stelrad is the UK's most-fitted rad brand. Their Elite range is the standard pick in most Liverpool homes. Quinn rads have a low water content which means faster heat-up times. Myson rads are made by the Finnish Purmo group. All three have good UK spare parts.</p>
        <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Stelrad</strong><p>UK heritage brand, founded 1936. The Elite range is the most-fitted panel rad in the UK. Good value, strong build, easy parts.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Quinn (formerly Barlo)</strong><p>Low water content means faster heat-up. Lower gas use overall. A good pick for energy efficient homes.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Myson / Purmo</strong><p>Made by the Finnish Purmo group. Strong on warranty. The Myson T6 is a popular pick.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h3 style="color:var(--navy);font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Designer: Reina, Hudson Reed and Bisque</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.6;">Designer rads from Reina, Hudson Reed and Bisque. Reina is the UK leader for towel rails and designer rads. Hudson Reed comes with a 10-year warranty on all rads. Bisque does high-end designer pieces. Vertical rads are good for rooms where horizontal wall space is tight.</p>
        <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Reina Design</strong><p>UK leader in designer rads and towel rails. Modern, sleek styles. The Casina and Diva ranges are popular picks.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Hudson Reed</strong><p>Diverse range with a 10-year warranty on every rad. Good mid to high-end pick.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Bisque</strong><p>High-end UK designer brand. Premium pricing. Best for main rooms in higher-end Liverpool homes.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h3 style="color:var(--navy);font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Period and Cast Iron Effect: Carron and Stelrad Column</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.6;">Period and cast iron effect rads from Carron and the Stelrad Column range. These suit Liverpool's Victorian and Edwardian homes well. They give the same heat output as a panel rad but look right with the period style. Best for living rooms, hallways and main bedrooms in older homes.</p>
        <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Carron</strong><p>Cast iron-style rads with the look of original Victorian rads. Modern build, period style. Sit well with old fireplaces and coving.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Stelrad Column range</strong><p>Steel column rads in two, three and four-column versions. Up to 1800mm tall for rooms with high ceilings.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;text-align:center;margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <p style="color:#ffffff;font-weight:700;font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Not sure which brand fits your home and budget? Please call us for a free quote today.</p>
