  <!-- NEW SECTION: ADDITIONAL RADIATORS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">ADDITIONAL RADIATORS</span>
      <h2>Adding a New Radiator to Your Liverpool System</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Need to add a new rad to your existing system? We do this every week across Liverpool. Most extensions and loft conversions need at least one extra rad.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Common reasons to add a radiator</strong><p>Common reasons to add a rad: a new extension. A loft conversion. A garage conversion. A conservatory. A cold corner of a big room. Or a room with no rad that should have one. We extend the circuit to the new spot and connect a new rad with a TRV.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>What is included in the job</strong><p>Adding one rad takes 2 to 4 hours. We drain the system, run new pipework to the new spot, fit the rad with a TRV and refill. We balance the whole system after. The job is done in one visit with minimal disruption to your home.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Power flush check first</strong><p>If your existing system is clogged, we suggest a power flush first. Without it, the new rad fills up with sludge fast. We check the system at the quote visit and tell you if a flush is needed. A flush plus a new rad in one visit is a better combined price.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Cost from £200 supply and fit</strong><p>A new rad added to your existing system costs from £200 supply and fit. This covers the rad, the TRV, all new pipework to the new spot and the system balance on the day. Multiple new rads can be done in a single visit at a better combined price.</p></div></div>
