      <h2>Thermostatic Radiator Valves for Liverpool Homes</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">A TRV on every rad is one of the most cost-effective heating upgrades you can do in a Liverpool home. The Boiler Plus rules need TRVs on all new installs.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-pros">
          <h3 style="text-align:center;">Why Every Liverpool Radiator Should Have a TRV</h3>
          <ul class="pf-check-list">
            <li>Sets the heat per room. The lounge runs warmer. The spare bedroom cooler. No heat wasted in rooms you do not use</li>
            <li>Cuts heating bills by 10 to 15%. The <a href="https://energysavingtrust.org.uk/advice/thermostats-and-heating-controls/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Energy Saving Trust</a> says TRVs in a Liverpool semi can save up to £75 a year</li>
            <li>A must under Boiler Plus rules on all new rad fits since 2018</li>
            <li>Stops south-facing Liverpool lounges from getting too hot in the sun</li>
            <li>Works with all modern boilers and smart thermostats</li>
            <li>Fitted from £50 per valve. A full house of TRV upgrades runs £150 to £300 and pays back in two winters</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-info-bar" style="margin-top:2rem;">
          <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text);">Note: one rad in the house (usually the hallway) should be left without a TRV to act as a bypass. This lets the boiler move water even when all other TRVs are shut. We always tell you about this when we fit TRVs across a full house.</p>
