        <h3>Solid Walls, Suspended Floors and Period Features</h3>
        <p>Liverpool's older homes have solid brick walls. No cavity. Horizontal pipe runs across solid walls go in boxing on the surface. Or under suspended timber floors where we can get under. Both work fine. We check each room at the quote visit and pick the neatest route.</p>
        <p>Suspended timber floors let us run pipes below without lifting carpet. Where floors are solid, we use neat boxing on the wall. We plan every route to keep period features safe. Coving and old skirting all left as they were.</p>
