      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>Choosing the Right Radiator Style for a Period Liverpool Home</h3>
        <p>Standard double panel rads work fine in older homes and give more heat for the price than column ones. If the look matters, column rads in two or four-column versions suit Victorian rooms well. They come in heights up to 1800mm for rooms with high ceilings.</p>
        <p>For Liverpool homes with big bay windows, a rad in the bay is the best way to fight cold air from the glass. We size the bay rad for the actual room, never just for what fits in the alcove. An undersized bay rad is one of the most common causes of cold front rooms in Liverpool Victorian terraces.</p>
