        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>You need a power flush first if...</strong><p>More than one of your existing rads has a cold spot at the bottom. The water from bleeding is brown or black. Your boiler bangs or kettles. The system takes ages to warm up. Any of these means sludge in the circuit that will fill new rads fast.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item" style="border-left:3px solid var(--green);"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:var(--green);">✓</span><div><strong>You do not need a flush if...</strong><p>Your existing rads all heat well. The system warms up fast. The water from bleeding is clear. In this case new rads can join the circuit straight away. We top up the inhibitor on the day.</p></div></div>
