      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does radiator installation cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A standard double panel rad, supplied and fitted, costs from £200. This covers the rad, the TRV and a system balance on the day. Labour only for a like-for-like swap starts at £80. TRVs from £50 each. Relocation from £150. Column and designer rads are quoted on request. We give a written fixed-price quote first.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TIME</span>&nbsp; How long does radiator installation take?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A like-for-like single radiator swap takes 1 to 2 hours. A new radiator addition with pipework takes 2 to 4 hours. Multiple radiators can often be completed in a single day. A full house TRV upgrade typically takes half a day. We confirm the expected duration when we quote.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">SIZING</span>&nbsp; Can you change a radiator to a bigger or smaller size?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We can swap an undersized rad for a bigger one to warm a cold room. Or fit a smaller rad in a room that gets too hot. We work out the BTU output the room needs first. Then we pick a rad that hits that number. A right-sized rad is more energy efficient. You burn less gas for the same warm room.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">ADDING</span>&nbsp; Can you add an additional radiator to my existing system?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Adding a rad to your existing system takes 2 to 4 hours. We extend the circuit to the new spot and fit the rad with a TRV. We balance the system after. Most extension, loft conversion and conservatory jobs need at least one extra rad.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">RELOCATION</span>&nbsp; Can you relocate a radiator in a Liverpool Victorian property?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We drain the circuit, reroute the pipework to the new spot and balance the system. Relocation starts from £150. Cost depends on distance. In older Liverpool homes with solid walls, pipes run under timber floors or in neat boxing on the wall.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TRV</span>&nbsp; What is a TRV and do I need one?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A TRV sets the heat output of one rad. Different rooms can run at different temps. Under Boiler Plus rules, TRVs are a must on all new rad fits. They cut heating bills by 10 to 15%. We fit TRVs from £50 per valve. One rad in the house should be left without a TRV to act as a bypass.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">FLUSH</span>&nbsp; Do I need a power flush before fitting new radiators?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>If your rads have cold spots at the bottom, or the water from bleeding is brown or black, a power flush is a must before fitting new rads. A clogged circuit will fill new rads with sludge fast. We check your system at the quote visit and tell you if a flush is needed.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">BRANDS</span>&nbsp; What radiator brands do you fit?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We fit rads from Stelrad, Quinn, Myson, Reina, Hudson Reed, Bisque and Carron. Standard panel rads, designer rads and period-style rads all in the range. We can supply the rad or fit one you have bought. Tell us your budget and style and we will help you pick.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is on the Gas Safe register. All rad work that joins the heating circuit is done by our own employed Gas Safe heating engineers. You can check us at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We never use sub-contractors.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

